      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "041b77c6c8d424dd30b69f8c314ea2e731bd131577c32468391a722bf2fc0d31",
      "text": "Day 10 · Breakfast at the hotel. Depart for Guatapé, one of Colombia’s most colourful and picturesque towns, known for its beautifully decorated façades and distinctive zócalos, traditional bas-relief panels depicting scenes from local life and culture. Continue to El Peñol Rock (La Piedra del Peñol), one of Antioquia’s most iconic natural landmarks. Rising nearly 220 metres above the surrounding landscape, the granite monolith offers panoramic views across a vast mosaic of lakes and islands.\n\nAfterwards, enjoy a leisurely stroll through Guatapé, taking in its colourful architecture, traditional details and lively lakeside atmosphere before returning to Medellín.",
